# ALWAYS ON - stable name for the Heltec V3 LoRa board.
#
# 2026-09-30: this rule previously matched on vendor/product alone
# (10c4:ea60). Both ALWAYS ON LoRa radios are CP2102 boards reporting the SAME
# generic ids and the SAME placeholder serial "_0001", so the rule fired on
# them and created /dev/heltec-v3 -> ttyUSB0, which is the DRONE-RADIO. Any
# consumer of that symlink would have talked to the drone radio's private
# Reticulum RNode.
#
# Fix: require a real, non-placeholder serial. Generic CP2102 clones report
# ID_SERIAL_SHORT=0001 and are excluded, so the two radios are never claimed.
# The Reticulum interfaces do not use this symlink at all - they address the
# radios by /dev/serial/by-path topology, which is unambiguous.
#
# Still to confirm when the Heltec is actually connected: its real by-path and
# serial. If it too reports 0001, this rule must be re-keyed on by-path instead.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}==="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", ENV{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}!="0001", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout", SYMLINK+="heltec-v3"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}==="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea71", ENV{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}!="0001", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout", SYMLINK+="heltec-v3"
